Faust standard libraries. The Faust sources under faust/ import the Faust
standard libraries (stdfaust.lib), which are not included in this source tree.
The default build's DSP (src/hydra_dsp_ref.c) is hand-written C, not Faust
output, and contains no generated library code. The optional
Faust backend (`make faust`, `nix build .#hydramodem-faust`) has the Faust
compiler inline library code into the C it generates, and the generated code
records each library's licence in its metadata. Generated with Faust 2.85.5
and its libraries, that metadata declares:

  - maths.lib (TX and RX): Copyright GRAME, "LGPL with exception" -- the
    LGPL-2.1-or-later plus GRAME's exception, which lets the compiled code be
    distributed under a licence of the distributor's choosing.
  - filters.lib dcblocker, pole and zero (TX only): Copyright (C) 2003-2019
    by Julius O. Smith III <jos@ccrma.stanford.edu>, "MIT-style STK-4.3
    license" (MIT terms plus a non-binding request to send modifications to
    the author). Its copyright and permission notice must accompany copies of
    the generated code.

The other libraries named in that metadata (platform.lib, signals.lib) carry
GRAME's same LGPL-with-exception header. The generated files are build output
and are not committed here.
